<title>ITALY: SWIMMING-PANKRATOV SETS WORLD 100 BUTTERFLY RECORD.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-PANKRATOV SETS WORLD 100 BUTTERFLY RECORD.</headline>
<dateline>IMPERIA, Italy 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denis Pankratov of Russia set a world record for the short-course men's 100 metres butterfly when he clocked 51.93 seconds at a World Cup meeting on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The previous best of 52.07 seconds was set by Marcel Gery of Canada in Leicester, England, on February 23, 1990.</p>
